SnailSynk for Debian
--------------------

Run `snailsynk` in a terminal (or use the menu entry). The first run asks a few
questions; after that it just starts. Data lives in ~/.local/share/snailsynk.

The AI chat needs the Google Gemini client, which Debian does not package. It is
optional: everything else works without it. To enable the chat, install it for
your user and add a GEMINI_API_KEY in the setup questions:

    pip install --user --break-system-packages google-genai

To remove your data after uninstalling the package, delete ~/.local/share/snailsynk
(notes are in its instance/notes folder) and ~/Downloads/SnailSynk.
